    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0313" n="1047" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1047"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Hicks.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 139.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 180, of November 3
                    last, concerning the claim of the Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon, I have
                    to say that before the opening of the Peruvian Congress, which, as stated in
                    your No. 180, will take place on July 28 next, it will be well to call the
                    attention of the foreign office to the claim, and to urge that it may be again
                    recommended to Congress.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
